MARKS SHEET GRADER

Marks Sheet Grader — a real-world task using only today's concepts: looping over a list, counting with variables, sum(), len(), building a list with append(), comparisons, if / elif / else, while validation, and printing. No imports, no tricks.

Solve it individually, then come together as a group to compare approaches. Good luck!

Bring back your Day 3 Report Card Grader scale - today the whole class gets graded at once.

- 70 to 100: A - Excellent
- 60 to 69: B - Very Good
- 50 to 59: C - Good
- 45 to 49: D - Pass
- 0 to 44: F - Fail

The program must:
- Ask "Scores for how many students: " and keep asking until it is at least 1.
- Ask for each score in order (Score 1: , Score 2: ...) and collect them into a list. (Assume scores are typed as whole numbers in range.)
- Then loop over the list and grade each score, printing one line per student: Score 82: B - PASS (D and above is a pass, F is a fail).
- Count the fails while looping.
- After the last one, print exactly two lines:
  CLASS AVERAGE: 61.40
  FAILED: 1

Sample run:

Scores for how many students: 3
Score 1: 82
Score 2: 43
Score 3: 70

Score 82: B - PASS
Score 43: F - FAIL
Score 70: A - PASS
CLASS AVERAGE: 65.00
FAILED: 1

Edge cases to handle: a single student, all students failing (FAILED shows everyone, average still prints), all passing, scores of exactly 44 then 45 (F then D - the pass boundary), and exactly 69 then 70 (B then A).
